{
 "_doc": "Firearm definitions. Times in seconds, angles in degrees, velocity m/s. recoil.kick_up/kick_side are per-shot weapon impulses; camera_share is the fraction of the kick that moves the view (the rest is weapon-only offset that recovers). climb is the extra upward bias added per consecutive shot, recovery is deg/s back toward the aim point, pattern lists horizontal bias multipliers cycled per shot so guns do not share one spray pattern. Attachments: kind is the slot (sight, muzzle, grip, mag, stock, light; one of each per weapon). *_mult fields multiply the weapon's value (recoil_up, recoil_side, recovery, spread_hip, move_spread, sway, ads_time, reload, loudness, flash, pellet_spread). ext switches to the weapon's mag_ext capacity. Sights: zoom; axis = optical axis height above the rail in metres (axis_f: fraction of the model height); reticle style; scope = magnified, drawn as a scope view while aiming. rank orders same-slot attachments when picking up. Weapons: value ranks weapons for bots; hold = [grip, fore-end] as fractions of the length from the muzzle, optionally followed by their heights as fractions of the model height; mounts overrides the automatic mount points.",
